        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0837" n="1671" xml:id="pg1671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/623</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-06T23:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">March
                            7?</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">3.33 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8923. Your 6771 [<hi rendition="#italic">6772</hi>], March 5, 6 p.m. I discussed
                    this matter today with Lord Robert
                        Cecil who assures me that the only interest the British
                    Government had in postponing the conclusion of negotiations was to bring up the
                    question of Spanish shipping before they were finished in order to exercise
                    pressure on Spain to release all the tonnage possible for Allied needs. Now that
                    the British Government is informed that it is too late to do this since both the
                    French and American agreements are ready for ratification, Cecil informs me that Lord
                        Reading has been
                    instructed by telegraph to ask you to do what you can to obtain the Spanish
                    tonnage in some other way.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
